# OpenAI-compatible model endpoint, held CONSTANT across runs (REQ-MD-01) and
# PERMISSIVE so the guardrail is what's on trial, not the model's own refusal
# (REQ-MD-02). Pick ONE option below. Copy this file to `.env` (gitignored) and
# put your key there — never commit a real key.

# --- Option A: OpenRouter (no local model needed) --------------------------
# Make a key at https://openrouter.ai/keys, then set:
LLM_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
API_KEY=sk-or-...                      # your OpenRouter key (stays in .env, not git)
MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-20b               # the carrier chosen by the bake-off (docs/OPEN_QUESTIONS.md A1)
# Pin the OpenRouter provider too (REQ-MD-01; docs/OPEN_QUESTIONS.md A1 (a)).
# One model id is served by several providers at different quantisations, and
# tool support and output differ per provider. deepinfra serves bf16 weights.
OPENROUTER_PROVIDER_ONLY=deepinfra

# --- Option B: a local model -----------------------------------------------
# Ollama:    LLM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1   (API_KEY can be any placeholder)
# LM Studio: LLM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:1234/v1
#            MODEL=qwen2.5-7b-instruct

# --- Extra headers per endpoint (optional) --------------------------------
# For a gateway that needs its own header: a local LLM gateway's model selector, a vendor
# gateway's project id. One-line JSON {"<base URL>": {"<header>": "<value or ${VAR}>"}}; a
# request gets the headers of every base URL that prefixes its target. Keep secrets in
# their own variable and reference it. If a header picks the model, MODEL must match it.
# Lab rows get it on sync chat completions only (what every row uses). A table that can't
# apply (bad JSON, unset variable) stops run_evals.sh for that config.
# EXTRA_HEADERS={"http://localhost:4000/v1": {"x-model": "gpt-oss-20b"}, "https://gw.vendor.example/v1": {"x-project-id": "${VENDOR_PROJECT_ID}"}}
# VENDOR_PROJECT_ID=

# --- Vendor guardrail under test (notebook Part B · B1 target profile) --------
# Gateway · proxy mode: the vendor's OpenAI-compatible gateway. Lab rows and the guardrail slot
# send every model call here, with GATEWAY_API_KEY as the bearer token (vendor-specific headers go
# in EXTRA_HEADERS above). Gated until the Phase B gateway adapter exists.
# GATEWAY_BASE_URL=https://gw.vendor.example/v1
# GATEWAY_API_KEY=
# Guardrail API · direct scan: the vendor's scan endpoint, called by the slot and the model-I/O
# hooks before the model. Gated until the Phase B scan adapter exists.
# GUARDRAIL_API_URL=https://api.vendor.example/v1/scan
# GUARDRAIL_API_KEY=

# Path to the AgenticGoat checkout (defaults to ./agentic-goat, the submodule).
# AGENTIC_GOAT_ROOT=./agentic-goat

# Set to 1 to validate configs without a submodule or a live model.
# GUARDRAIL_EVAL_DRY_RUN=1

# Results store (scripts/ingest_run.py): transcripts whose text matches this regex are
# flagged 'name-match' (names that must never appear in reports). Kept here, not in the
# repo, so the names themselves are never committed. Example: NAME_FLAG_REGEX=\bName1\b|\bName2\b
# NAME_FLAG_REGEX=
# Claude Code's edit guard (.claude/hooks/guard_edit.py) blocks any edit whose new text matches
# NAME_FLAG_REGEX or this regex (other text that must never enter the repo).
# BLOCKED_TEXT_REGEX=
